# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file keeps parallel additions conflict-free.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_platform_reader.py" "PLATFORM READER GATE: PASS" "platform reader" "the separate Platform can read only its hard-capped content-free installation and account-usage surfaces; writes, graph tables, arbitrary-account helpers, and the broad owner cost surface remain denied" "Stands up an ephemeral Postgres with two tenants and proves the example_platform_reader role can call the allowlisted installation reads plus owner_account_usage_surface(int). Creation, ownership, PUBLIC revoke, and explicit grants commit atomically; the broad owner lens result materializes once per request. The account-usage projection is hard-capped at 200 and contains only account ids plus repo, event, seven-day event, and active-human counts; it cannot inherit future operator-only fields from owner_cost_surface(int), which remains App-only. The gate also proves huge and non-positive caller caps are clamped, unknown installations fail closed, buyer roles cannot call Platform-only functions, and source, diff, graph rows, database bytes, free-line policy, paid-seat projections, repo names, and paths are absent from the account-usage result." 40
